## Why there is a separate migration tool project

The MAUI app project (`src/Bible.Alarm`) deliberately does **not** include EF “design-time” tooling packages.

Instead, migrations are managed via:
- `.tools/Bible.Alarm.DbMigration/` (console + design-time factories)

This keeps MAUI runtime dependencies clean and makes EF CLI operations predictable.

---

## Where migrations live

Migrations are generated into the Shared project:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/Migrations/Schedule/**`
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/Migrations/Media/**`

The DbContexts are in:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/ScheduleDbContext.cs`
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/MediaDbContext.cs`

The migrations assembly for both contexts is configured as:
- `"Bible.Alarm.Shared"` (see DI registration in `ServiceRegistrationHelper.cs`)

---

## Common commands (developer workflow)

### Create a migration

Schedule DB:

```bash
dotnet ef migrations add <MigrationName> --project .tools/Bible.Alarm.DbMigration --context ScheduleDbContext --output-dir ../src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/Migrations/Schedule
```

Media DB:

```bash
dotnet ef migrations add <MigrationName> --project .tools/Bible.Alarm.DbMigration --context MediaDbContext --output-dir ../src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Database/Migrations/Media
```

### Apply migrations to a local DB (for testing)

```bash
dotnet ef database update --project .tools/Bible.Alarm.DbMigration --context ScheduleDbContext
dotnet ef database update --project .tools/Bible.Alarm.DbMigration --context MediaDbContext
```

